# =============================================================================

# .dockerignore — React Frontend (Vite + TypeScript)

# =============================================================================

# The frontend Dockerfile has two stages:

# Stage 1 (builder): runs "pnpm install" then "pnpm build" → produces /dist

# Stage 2 (nginx): copies only /dist into the Nginx image

#

# The most important exclusion is node_modules/ — it can be 300MB–1GB and

# must NEVER be copied in. The builder stage runs its own "npm ci" inside

# the container, creating a clean, reproducible install from scratch.

# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Node modules — THE most critical exclusion

# node_modules/ on your machine is built for your host OS (macOS/Windows).

# The Docker container runs Linux — binary packages (like esbuild, rollup)

# would be the wrong platform and fail. "npm ci" inside the container builds

# the correct Linux-compatible versions automatically.

# Copying it in would also add 300MB–1GB to the build context for no benefit.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

node_modules/ .npm/ .pnpm-store/ .yarn/ .pnp.\*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Vite build output

# The builder stage runs "npm run build" inside the container to create /dist.

# Your local /dist folder (if it exists) is stale and should never be used —

# the container always builds fresh.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

dist/ dist-ssr/ build/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Vite and TypeScript cache

# These are runtime caches for faster local rebuilds. Irrelevant inside Docker

# since the container always starts from scratch.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

.vite/ .vite-cache/ \*.tsbuildinfo tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Environment and secrets

# CRITICAL: .env files often contain API keys, backend URLs, and feature flags.

# Vite bakes VITE\_\* variables into the bundle at build time — but the source

# .env file itself should never exist inside the image.

# Pass build-time variables via ARG/ENV in the Dockerfile or docker-compose args.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

.env .env.\* \*.env !.env.example

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Test files and coverage

# Tests run in CI, not in the production Nginx image. Excluding them keeps

# the build context clean and prevents test utilities from accidentally being

# bundled (though Vite tree-shaking would catch most of this anyway).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

**/**tests**/ **/_.test.ts \*\*/_.test.tsx **/\*.spec.ts **/\*.spec.tsx coverage/ .nyc_output/ test-results/ playwright-report/ cypress/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Storybook

# Component development environment — not needed in the production build.

# Can be several hundred MB including its own node_modules and build cache.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

.storybook/ storybook-static/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# IDE and editor files

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# VS Code

.vscode/ \*.code-workspace

# IntelliJ / WebStorm

.idea/ \*.iml

# Generic

_.swp _.swo _~ _.bak

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OS-generated files

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# macOS

.DS*Store .DS_Store? .*\* .Spotlight-V2 .Trashes

# Windows

Thumbs.db ehthumbs.db Desktop.ini

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Git

# The full Git history is not needed to serve static files. Can be 50-500MB

# on active projects.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

.git/ .gitignore .gitattributes

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Docker files themselves

# No need to include build configuration inside the built image.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Dockerfile Dockerfile._ .dockerignore docker-compose_.yml

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Logs

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

logs/ _.log npm-debug.log_ yarn-debug.log* yarn-error.log* pnpm-debug.log\*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Documentation

# README, architecture docs, and design assets don't affect the Nginx server

# or the bundled JS/CSS output.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

_.md README_ docs/ CHANGELOG* LICENSE*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# DevOps / CI config

# If the frontend lives in a monorepo root, exclude infra files that have

# nothing to do with building the React app.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

.github/ terraform/ ansible/ k8s/ helm/ scripts/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Backend (if in same repo)

# Prevents the entire Spring Boot project from being sent to the frontend

# Docker build context.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

backend/ src/main/ src/test/ pom.xml mvnw mvnw.cmd .mvn/
